        <item>
            <title>0.15.86</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:21:48 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>247</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.86</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.2</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
<li>Very long recordings (over about three hours) are saved in full. Recording audio now takes half the disk space, and a file can no longer become unreadable past 4 GB.</li>
<li>If the other side&#x27;s audio stops coming through mid-call (for example after the audio system restarts), Corder reconnects to it, keeps both sides in sync, and warns you if it can&#x27;t.</li>
<li>If your microphone stops delivering sound mid-recording, Corder reconnects to it on its own.</li>
<li>Fixed a rare crash when switching audio devices during a recording.</li>
<li>Creating a share link for a long meeting no longer freezes Corder while the audio is prepared.</li>
<li>Corder stays responsive while a long recording is being processed after you stop it.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
